From: Smartisan ODIN mainline porting effort
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] lk2nd: go to fastboot instead of booting the stale android image

When lk2nd fails to boot from any file system it currently just logs
"Reverting to android boot." and returns, letting aboot fall through to
boot_linux_from_mmc().

On ODIN that fallback is harmful: the 'boot' partition still carries the
stock android boot image at offset 512 KB (lk2nd itself lives in the
first 512 KB, exposed by fastboot as a separate 'lk2nd' partition). That
image is booted, finds no system partition and reboots -- and lk2nd then
repeats the whole thing, so the device reboot-loops until someone holds
the power button. That makes the flash/reboot cycle impossible to automate.

Fix it in two places:

- lk2nd/boot/boot.c: set boot_into_fastboot once we fall off the end of
  lk2nd_scan_devices(). Reaching that point already means nothing was
  booted (a successful boot jumps into the kernel and never returns), so
  no return value needs to be threaded through.

- app/aboot/aboot.c: re-check boot_into_fastboot right after lk2nd_boot()
  and jump to the fastboot label. The existing check happens *before*
  lk2nd_boot() runs, so without this the flag would be ignored and we
  would still fall through to the android image.

With this, disabling extlinux.conf -- our standard way of getting into
fastboot -- lands in fastboot directly instead of reboot-looping.

Verified on device:
  offset 0      of /dev/mmcblk0p21 -> "ANDROID!" (lk2nd)
  offset 524288 of /dev/mmcblk0p21 -> "ANDROID!" (stale stock image)
  getvar: partition-size:lk2nd = 0x80000, partition-size:boot = 0x3f80000

Note the other lk2nd_boot() call site (aboot.c ~4674, inside the
target_is_emmc_boot() branch) still falls through to the android image.
It is not on the path we use, and is left alone to keep this change small.
---
--- a/lk2nd/boot/boot.c
+++ b/lk2nd/boot/boot.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <lib/bio.h>
 #include <lib/fs.h>
 #include <list.h>
+#include <stdbool.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <target.h>
 
@@ -13,12 +14,22 @@
 
 #include "boot.h"
 
+/*
+ * aboot.c 里的全局标志。lk2nd 没能从文件系统引导时置位，
+ * 让 aboot 直接进 fastboot，而不是回退去引导 boot 分区里残留的
+ * Android 镜像（见下面 lk2nd_scan_devices() 末尾的说明）。
+ */
+extern bool boot_into_fastboot;
+
 #ifndef LK2ND_BOOT_MIN_SIZE
 #define LK2ND_BOOT_MIN_SIZE (16 * 1024 * 1024)
 #endif
 
 /**
  * lk2nd_scan_devices() - Scan filesystems and try to boot
+ *
+ * 注意：能从这个函数的末尾正常返回，就意味着**什么都没引导起来** ——
+ * 引导成功是要跳进内核的，不会返回。所以末尾那段不需要任何返回值来判断。
  */
 static void lk2nd_scan_devices(void)
 {
@@ -60,7 +71,22 @@
 		lk2nd_try_extlinux(mountpoint);
 	}
 
-	dprintf(INFO, "boot: Bootable file system not found. Reverting to android boot.\n");
+	/*
+	 * 走到这里说明没有任何文件系统被引导起来（引导成功会跳进内核，不返回）。
+	 *
+	 * 上游的默认行为是打一行日志就返回，让 aboot 继续去引导 boot 分区里的
+	 * Android 镜像。在 ODIN 上这条回退是**有害的**：boot 分区偏移 512KB 处
+	 * 还留着原厂的 Android 引导镜像，它会真的被引导起来，然后因为找不到
+	 * system 分区而重启 —— 于是设备陷入 lk2nd → Android → 重启 的死循环，
+	 * 只能人工长按电源键打断，整个刷机/调试流程无法自动跑完。
+	 *
+	 * 这里改为置 boot_into_fastboot，由 aboot 跳到 fastboot 标签（见
+	 * app/aboot/aboot.c 里 lk2nd_boot() 之后的那个判断）。
+	 * 效果：把 extlinux.conf 改名（我们进入 fastboot 的标准手法）之后，
+	 * 设备会干净地停在 fastboot，不再反复重启。
+	 */
+	dprintf(INFO, "boot: Bootable file system not found. Reverting to fastboot.\n");
+	boot_into_fastboot = true;
 }
 
 /**
--- a/app/aboot/aboot.c
+++ b/app/aboot/aboot.c
@@ -5655,6 +5655,18 @@
 #if WITH_LK2ND_BOOT
 		if (!boot_into_recovery)
 			lk2nd_boot();
+
+		/*
+		 * lk2nd 没能从文件系统引导起来时，会置 boot_into_fastboot
+		 * （见 lk2nd/boot/boot.c 末尾）。
+		 *
+		 * 这里的重新判断**不能省**：上面那个 if (!boot_into_fastboot)
+		 * 在 lk2nd_boot() 之前就已经判过了，不重判就会继续往下走，
+		 * 去引导 boot 分区偏移 512KB 处残留的原厂 Android 镜像 ——
+		 * 它会起不来并重启，于是设备在 lk2nd 与 Android 之间反复重启。
+		 */
+		if (boot_into_fastboot)
+			goto fastboot;
 #endif
 
 		if (target_is_emmc_boot())
